<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Code-to-model traceability: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every function docstring states V, S, and the resulting formula (L68-110), and the module header table (L25-30) maps shapes to scaling predictions and cites Appendix A / Results (L66), Fig. 6 (L60, L156), and Fig. 3 (L187). Deduct points because no specific equation numbers from Appendix A are given and the annual forward-Euler discretization is not traced to a specific equation in the paper." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Model fidelity to source: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The master rule V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho (L15-16, L64-67) and the four shape derivations (hemisphere L68-78, disc L81-89, cone L92-104, cylinder L107-110) are algebraically exact for a 1-year discrete step. However, the discrete annual step introduces a time-step artifact presented as geometry: hemisphere_extension (L70) and panel (c) (L173-182) show C rising from 0.52 cm/yr at r = 0.5 cm toward a plateau G/rho = 1.25 cm/yr, whereas in the continuous model dV/dt = 2*pi*r^2*dr/dt = G*(2*pi*r^2)/rho implies dr/dt = G/rho identically for all r (and the discrete disc extension is ~30% below continuum at G/(rho*h) = 2.5). In addition, upper-surface-only disc S (L82), baseless cone S (L93-94), and single-cylinder branching (L107-110) are not explicitly stated as simplifying assumptions." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Morphometric validation: 22/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script prints G/rho = 1.28 cm/yr for massive Porites (L252), the ~19x microfragmentation SAP ratio between r = 1 cm and r = 25 cm (L231, L263), and Leptoseris SAP = 0.114 yr^-1 (L258), but never compares them against observed coral extension or fragment growth tables (Lough 2008, Hughes 1987, Kahng 2023), and computes no fit, residual, or observed-vs-model validation metric." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-branching-acropora-cylinder-size-independent-sap-r-0-50-cm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-deep-water-leptoseris-flat-disc-size-independent-sap-h-0-20-cm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-massive-porites-hemisphere-linear-extension-c-at-r-30-cm-discrete-1-yr-step>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-massive-porites-microfragmentation-sap-speedup-ratio-r-1-cm-vs-r-25-cm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 2.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-overall-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — MorphoEval overall 49.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Blinded second-assessor pass. The script encodes Kahng, Odle & Wakeman's (2024) accounting rule — skeleton volume grows by G*S/rho per step — and derives, for four idealised shapes (hemisphere, fixed-aspect cone, fixed-thickness disc, fixed-radius cylinder), the one-step linear extension and surface-area productivity (dS/S). The algebra for V(t+1) -> size(t+1) is correct for every shape, and the qualitative conclusions match the paper. However, the script's annual forward-Euler step makes hemisphere extension look size-dependent (0.52 cm/yr at r = 0.5 cm rising to 1.25 cm/yr), whereas the continuous geometry gives C = G/rho at every size; the 'equal G, rho' comparison applies G = 1.5 g cm^-2 yr^-1 to a 0.5 cm plate (yielding 26 cm/yr extension at r = 30 cm and S ~ 10^9 cm^2 after 15 years in the GIF); and no measured coral growth data are compared with the model output. Overall 49.1/100 (faithfulness 42.9, reproducibility 63.7; model-implementation 64.0/100, biological-validation 27.0/100, applicable-only overall 49.1/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 30, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 22, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 58, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py at 5564750, image/png, 282553 B, 1774×1267 px, artifact_sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812 (sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812), spec_fingerprint 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; artifact_sha256: fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:57-59 — Vendor empirical coral extension/calcification tables from Lough (2008), Hughes (1987), and Kahng (2023) in datasets/kahng/ with full DOIs and SHA-256 digests, and compare model C and SAP against observed colony growth.",
        "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:60,160-178 — Use biologically realistic DISC parameters in panel (c) so a 0.5 cm plate does not extend at 26 cm/yr and obscure the hemisphere and cone curves.",
        "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:68-110,173-182 — Separate continuous differential rates (hemisphere dr/dt = G/rho identically; cone dh/dt = G*sqrt(1+alpha^2)/rho; disc dr/dt = G*r/(2*rho*h)) from the discrete 1-yr Euler step, and expose dt as a parameter." ;
    pk:hasScore 4.91e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-parameter-expressivity-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Parameter expressivity: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Cone aspect ratio alpha monotonically raises cone SAP (panel d, L189-196), branch diameter and plate thickness monotonically lower SAP (panel e, L199-211), and colony size monotonically lowers hemisphere/cone SAP (panel b). However, applying the COMMON parameter set (G=1.50, rho=1.20, L60) to a 0.5 cm disc gives SAP = 2.5 yr^-1 and extension 26 cm/yr at r = 30 cm (panel c), which dominates the vertical axis and compresses the hemisphere and cone curves; panel (e) conflates branch diameter and plate thickness on a single x-axis (L201-207); and step size dt is not exposed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-repro-package-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Reproducibility package: 64/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic (no RNG), backed by requirements.lock.txt, with CLI flags at L320-331. However, --gif (L326) is omitted from the documented 'Run it' block (L38-41), show=True is the default (L327), GIF rendering via buffer_rgba (L312) is backend/font dependent, Pillow deduplicates the trailing hold frames (L314) from 24 to 16 frames on disk, and there is no self-test." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
