<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 30/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Spacing law diffusion_length (L64-67) is the correct form, but alpha and tau are free knobs set by the script (alpha_field = 1.0 at L179, alpha_lab = 0.30 at L180 described as a least-squares fit with no data or fit in the file), and the text panel states that 0.66 cm records a ~20 h rhythmic metabolism (L238-239) whereas 0.66 cm was computed at tau = 12 h (L193, L207; tau = 20 h gives 0.85 cm). Panels (d-f) and the GIF do not implement Petroff's diffusion-limited growth: they credit Batchelor et al. 2004 (L31-34, L86-98), modify it with an unsourced quadratic crest weight w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2 (L126-130) and 3-point smoothing (L141-142), and never integrate the docstring's own KPZ equation dh/dt = v + lambda*(1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2) (L34, L85, L296)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-morphometric-validation-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Morphometric validation: 15/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Only one morphometric is computed, aspect_ratio (L165-171), which the docstring notes is used only to annotate the figure, and it is compared with nothing measured. The shaded 0.5-1.5 cm band (L198) stands in for the paper's measured spacing distributions without data, and no lamina-thickness, apex-angle, or crest-zone-width metric is computed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-measurement-cone-regime-beta-1-5-final-lamina-height-width-aspect-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-measurement-dome-regime-beta-0-3-final-lamina-height-width-aspect-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-measurement-field-cone-spacing-ell-at-tau-12-h-d-1e-5-cm-2-s-alpha-1-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-measurement-sharp-cone-regime-beta-5-0-final-lamina-height-width-aspect-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 1.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "not faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-overall-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — MorphoEval overall 34.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Blinded second-assessor pass. The script reproduces one scalar relation from Petroff et al. (2010), ell = alpha*sqrt(D*tau), plots it against tau with two script-chosen alpha values, draws a hexagonal lattice of harvest disks at ell(tau=12 h) ~ 0.66 cm, and prints a verbal 'reading the fossil' panel. The lower half of the figure and the GIF are not Petroff's model: they integrate a Lagrangian front advanced by v*z_hat + lambda*n_hat (attributed in the code to Batchelor et al. 2004), multiplied by an ad hoc crest-weighting w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2, with Laplacian smoothing, a pinned base, and a triangular seed. Petroff et al.'s actual shape argument is nutrient-flux limited (quasi-steady diffusion field around neighbouring cones, mat growth set by local diffusive flux), and the paper's evidence is measured cone-spacing distributions from modern Yellowstone mats, laboratory cultures, and Proterozoic/Archean fossils; none of those data or that model appear here. Overall 34.0/100 (faithfulness 27.5, reproducibility 49.1; model-implementation 38.3/100, biological-validation 19.4/100, applicable-only overall 34.0/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 30, Morphological realism / specimen match 22, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 15, Source and data traceability 45, Code-to-model traceability 35, Reproducibility package 62. Output judged: petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py at 5564750, image/png, 328721 B, 1736×1244 px, artifact_sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01 (sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01), spec_fingerprint 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; artifact_sha256: 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:136-137 — Release the pinned basal footprint so beta < 1 produces a convex domal stromatolite rather than a vertical-walled trapezoid.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:193,207,238-239 — Make tau = 12 h (ell = 0.66 cm) and the '~20 h rhythmic metabolism' text panel consistent, and vendor measured modern/lab/fossil cone-spacing distributions and a Conophyton thin-section outline in datasets/petroff/.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:86-163 — Solve nabla^2 c = 0 around a periodic array of absorbing mats and grow the surface at a rate proportional to local diffusive flux dc/dn, rather than substituting a modified Batchelor front with ad-hoc w_photic (L126-130)." ;
    pk:hasScore 3.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Parameter expressivity: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "beta monotonically controls height/width (0.63 to 3.03 across beta = 0.2 to 6.0 in the GIF sweep at L300-334 and regimes at L249-253), and tau monotonically controls ell (L187-192). However, apex sharpness and flank slope are constrained by the pinned footprint (L136-137) and smooth (L141-142, L146); lambda is fixed at 1 throughout (L248, L305); and seed_height, base_half, smooth, and t_total (L146-147) are hidden parameters with no CLI exposure." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-repro-package-second-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Reproducibility package: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic (no RNG), backed by requirements.txt and requirements.lock.txt, with CLI flags documented at L336-348. However, --gif is omitted from the 'Run it' docstring block (L45-48), show=True is the default (L344), GIF capture via fig.canvas.buffer_rgba() (L329) is font/backend dependent, and there is no self-test." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
